Snowsky Disc emulation: device ioctls for static guest programs, SO_ERROR errno
================================================================================

Against Debian's qemu 7.2+dfsg-7+deb12u18 (the pinned qemu-user-static), after
its own patch series; built by emulator/docker/Dockerfile into
/usr/local/bin/qemu-mipsel-static. Two changes to linux-user/syscall.c:

* do_ioctl: while the guest's /emu/qemu-devices marker holds "1", ioctls on the
  REGULAR FILES /dev/fb0 and /dev/input/event* are answered with the emulated
  framebuffer (360x360x32, three sub-buffers; FBIOPAN_DISPLAY publishes
  /emu/fb-live) and input devices (name from the guest's sysfs stub; EVIOCGBIT,
  EVIOCGABS 0..359 for the panel, EVIOCGID, EVIOCGRAB ...). Dynamically linked
  programs get the same answers from the preloaded emulator/shims/fbshim.c; a
  statically linked program (a boot-layer package) only reaches the kernel, which
  says ENOTTY for a regular file. Character devices and other files are untouched.
  Paths go through qemu's path(), so -L <sysroot> applies (emulator/tests/test_devices.py).

* do_getsockopt: SO_ERROR is translated to the guest's errno numbering like the
  syscall errnos are (MIPS ECONNREFUSED is 146, not the host's 111).

See emulator/docs/stock-init.md (static programs) and emulator/docs/limits.md.

